  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "1tfrh9o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Sources of Ancient Indian History"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Indian History is reconstructed through archaeological finds and literary sources.",
        "The Prehistoric Period tracks human evolution through Stone Age phases.",
        "The Indus Valley Civilization is recognized for its sophisticated urban planning and drainage systems.",
        "Major sites such as Harappa, Mohenjo-daro, Lothal, and Kalibangan highlight significant economic and cultural aspects.",
        "Understanding the economy, religious practices, and reasons for decline of the IVC is vital for exam preparation."
      ],
      "id": "unor0o3"
    },
